  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The ionization energy of gaseous <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Na</mi></math> atoms is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>495</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The lowest possible frequency of light that ionizes a sodium atom is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mtext>h</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>6.626</mtext><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>Js</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mo>N</mo><mtext>A</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>6.022</mtext><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mo>mol</mo><mn>-1</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></math></p>",
